# Artifacts Directory — {{name}}

Research output artifacts organized by wave. Each wave produces specific deliverables into its own subdirectory. Gate checks validate the structure and content of these files.

## Directory map

| Directory | Produced by | Contents |
|-----------|-------------|----------|
| `wave0/` | Wave 0 | Per-topic thin YAML source lists (`<topic-slug>/source.yaml`) |
| `wave1/` | Wave 1 | Per-topic deepening (`<topic-slug>/evidence-summary.md`, `<topic-slug>/question-list.md`) |
| `wave2/` | Wave 2 | Cross-topic synthesis (`synthesis.md`, `cross-topic-ledger.md`, `finding-index.yaml`) |
| `hitl2/` | HITL2 | Final review decision brief (`decision-brief.md`) |

## Why no `hitl1/`?

HITL1 writes to root-level control files, not to `artifacts/`:
- `rb_plan.md` — original topic (body) + topic_registry (frontmatter)
- `rb_profile.yaml` — research_profile, root_must_answer_set, hitl1 status marker

There is no separate HITL1 artifact because the output IS the plan and profile.

## Per-wave detail

### wave0/

```
artifacts/wave0/<topic-slug>/source.yaml
```

One thin YAML file per topic from the `topic_registry`. Each file is an array of objects with fields: `url`, `title`, `retrieved_date` (YYYY-MM-DD), `topic_tag` (must match the topic slug), optional `notes`.

Source discovery also produces rich-Markdown reference files in `reference/00-shared-*.md` (flat directory, not under `artifacts/`).

### wave1/

```
artifacts/wave1/<topic-slug>/evidence-summary.md
artifacts/wave1/<topic-slug>/question-list.md
```

- `evidence-summary.md` — deepened evidence narrative with source URL links in Markdown format. Must contain `## Key Findings` with at least one `[text](https://...)` link per collected source.
- `question-list.md` — four required sections: `## Topic Investigation Targets`, `## Question Reconciliation`, `## Emergent Question Protocol`, `## Exploration / Exploitation Decision`.

Per-topic source deepening also produces rich-Markdown reference files in `reference/0N-*.md` (where N is the topic's id number).

### wave2/

```
artifacts/wave2/synthesis.md
artifacts/wave2/cross-topic-ledger.md
artifacts/wave2/finding-index.yaml
```

- `synthesis.md` — cross-topic narrative. Must contain `W2F-xxx` finding ID references and Markdown links to wave1 `.md` artifacts.
- `cross-topic-ledger.md` — six required sections: `## Cross-Topic Scan Matrix`, `## Wave1 Legacy Questions`, `## Cross-Topic Resolutions`, `## Emergent Cross-Topic Questions`, `## Exploration Decisions`, `## HITL2 Handoff`.
- `finding-index.yaml` — machine-readable taxonomy. Each entry has `finding_id`, `category` (legacy/resolution/emergent), `statement`, `sources`, `confidence`, `decision`.

Emergent cross-topic sources may also produce `reference/00-cross-*.md` files.

### hitl2/

```
artifacts/hitl2/decision-brief.md
```

Final review decision brief for human HITL2 review. Contains key findings summary, open questions, and recommended actions.

